"help.title" = "Connection scope and usage";
"help.steps" = "1. Choose apps. 2. Add proxy profiles and assign them. 3. Start network routing and approve the macOS prompt. Stop before editing rules. Stopping disconnects existing connections handled by the core.";
"help.tcp" = "TCP: SOCKS5 and HTTP CONNECT are supported. Identified matching connections fail when their proxy fails. Unknown processes connect directly; this app does not guarantee leak prevention.";
"help.helpers" = "Helpers: processes inside the .app bundle match by default. Shared WebKit networking, system services and other proxy tools outside the bundle cannot automatically be attributed to the originating app. Re-select an app after moving or updating it.";
"help.udp" = "UDP / QUIC: UDP from matching apps is rejected, allowing compatible clients to fall back to TCP. Unmatched UDP connects directly, including traffic from shared or unknown processes.";
"help.dns" = "DNS: system DNS settings stay unchanged and port 53 connects directly. Per-app DNS and DNS privacy are not provided. An app's own TCP DoH / DoT connections still follow its process rules.";
"help.ipv6" = "IPv6: the TUN configuration includes both IPv4 and IPv6. Live interception and restoration require administrator acceptance testing. Loopback, local links, explicitly bound interfaces and higher-priority VPN routes can bypass TUN.";
"help.lifecycle" = "Network state: core outbound sockets bind to the detected original interface. Verified local upstream processes and their entire app bundles take priority and connect directly to avoid loops; exceptions appear in the logs. Startup is refused if the local listener cannot be verified. Restart the session after its process restarts. Stopping compares routes and DNS without overwriting other network tools' settings.";
"help.license" = "This build is locally ad-hoc signed and is not notarized. No Apple Developer account is required. The app includes sing-box 1.14.3 (GPL-3.0-or-later), its license and source links.";
